`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The trickiest part of this ticket wasn't the code — there was none to write, since mrr-4z4.5 already wired the exec dispatch — it was proving the suspend/resume handoff actually works. Two agent-tui behaviors made this non-obvious: `wait` matches against scrollback rather than the live screen (so a phrase the fixture printed minutes ago can still "pass" an assertion), and separate tool calls introduce enough latency to race past a short-lived child process. Chaining the trigger keypress and screenshot into one shell command, plus giving the fixture a deliberate `sleep`, turned an unreliable check into a real one — this is a general lesson for testing any terminal-takeover primitive (`tea.ExecProcess`, `pty.Start`, etc.), not just mrboard-specific.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

